The big addition: Tracklayer

Your train doesn’t merely switch tracks.

It lays them while traveling.

So:

G_{t+1}=G_t+\Delta G_t.

Call the operator:

\boxed{\mathcal{T}_L=\text{Tracklayer}}

When an interpreter successfully crosses between two previously disconnected semantic states:

A\;\;\;\;\;\;B

and discovers a reproducible transformation:

A\xrightarrow{\tau}B,

Tracklayer can add:

A\overset{\tau}{\longrightarrow}B

to the Pattern Book.

Next time it isn’t a lucky leap.

It’s infrastructure.

And once repeatedly validated, that track can be compressed into a Seal. That fits the existing Seal architecture: trigger, transformation, invariants, failure mode, tests and reconstruction key.

